HYBRID-004 — Auth UX Review & Language Audit

Type: HYBRID (Agent + Human)
Sprint: Sprint 2
Owner: Agent (implementation complete), Alex (UX governor review)
Depends on: AGENTIC-003 — Authentication (S2-001)
Status: Blocked until AGENTIC-003 complete

🎯 Intent

Validate that the authentication experience introduced in Sprint 2:

Preserves FractPath’s exploratory, non-binding posture

Does not introduce accidental commitment semantics

Aligns with the Sprint 2 UX Intent Doc

This ticket exists to catch meaning drift, not bugs.

🧭 Review Scope (What This Ticket Covers)

This ticket reviews only:

Authentication-related copy

Page titles, buttons, helper text

Transitional language around login / logout

Implied user promises (what auth “means”)

This ticket does not:

Add new functionality

Change auth providers

Modify flows beyond copy/labels

Introduce new pages or logic

🔍 UX Audit Checklist (Governor Review)

Review the auth experience against the following:

1. Commitment Framing

 Auth feels like “remember me” or “pick up where you left off”

 No language implies application, approval, or submission

 No implication that the user has started a deal

2. Language Audit (Hard Rules)

Must NOT appear anywhere:

“Apply”

“Submit”

“Get approved”

“Lock in”

“Create a deal”

“Finalize”

“Offer”

Preferred language examples:

“Sign in to continue exploring”

“Save what you’ve been exploring”

“Welcome back”

(Exact wording may vary, meaning must match.)

3. Identity Semantics

 Logging in feels reversible and low-pressure

 Logging out feels safe (no loss framing)

 Auth does not feel like a point of no return

4. UX Intent Doc Alignment

Confirm alignment with:

Scenario ≠ Deal

Exploration before obligation

Identity continuity without commitment

If any auth surface contradicts these, it must be corrected.

✅ Acceptance Criteria

This ticket is complete when:

 All auth-related copy has been reviewed

 Any commitment-leaning language is removed or softened

 No new UX scope is introduced

 Sprint 2 UX Intent Doc is fully honored

📦 Deliverable

One of the following outcomes must be recorded in the ticket:

✅ Approved as-is

✏️ Approved with minor copy changes (list exact changes)

❌ Rejected due to semantic drift (explain why)

No screenshots or verbose commentary required unless helpful.

⚠️ Common Failure Modes (Reject If Seen)

Auth framed as a “next step” toward a deal

Language implying seriousness or eligibility

UX that pressures users to complete anything

“Sign up to get started” copy without context

🧠 Governor’s Note

This ticket exists to ensure Sprint 2 increases trust without increasing obligation.

If auth feels heavier than exploration, the sprint has failed its UX intent — even if the code works.
